cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying data, please cite the dataset record and this repository as below."
title: "adam2: counting graceful permutations of paths, with endpoint-resolved counts"
abstract: >-
  Programs for counting graceful permutations of the path graph P_n
  (OEIS A006967). adam2_v3.cpp is an Adamaszek-style layered
  dynamic-programming counter that can also restore the
  endpoint-resolved counts G(n; a, b) from its final layer;
  graceful_enum.c and graceful_enum_shard.c are an independent complete
  enumeration used as a cross-check for small n. The data/ directory
  mirrors the endpoint-resolved dataset archived on Zenodo.
authors:
  - family-names: Moriyama
    given-names: Masaru
date-released: 2026-10-30
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/Moriyamax/graceful-path-endpoints"
